maya (Support): FYI customer vouch reported function/tool call failures after switching to an OpenAI-compatible agent. multiple 4xx schema errors, 1st seen ~10:12 UTC :eyes:

maya (Support): payload attached from customer — they say it used to work with our hosted endpoint and now fails when routed through their openai-proxy. summary: tool selected but args treated as string, plus enum value unrecognized.

maya (Support): curl they used:
```
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/respond \ 
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk_cust' \ 
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ 
  -d '{"model":"gpt-4o-mini","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"send invoice"}],"tool_calls":[{"tool":{"id":"email.send","name":"send_email"},"arguments":"<data>{\"to\":\"acct+pay@example.com\",\"amount\":1000}</data>","intent":"immediate_retry"}]}'
```

maya (Support): Response from our API: 400 Bad Request
```
{"error":{"message":"tool_call.arguments: expected object, got string","code":"invalid_tool_args","details":"arguments must be a JSON object for tool 'email.send'"}}
```

kevin (Support): @derek can you triage? customer is P2 (billing flow) and still blocked. they saw this after enabling an openai proxy that wraps tool args as XML-escaped strings.

derek (Eng): Repro steps please — did they send Content-Type application/json? looks like args arrived as a string literal. also that enum `immediate_retry` vs our expected `IMMEDIATE` could be causing tool routing mismatch. can you paste raw request body from our ingress logs?

maya (Support): pasted raw request from ingress (sanitized):
```
{"tool_calls":[{"tool":{"id":"email.send","name":"send_email"},"arguments":"<payload>{\"to\":\"acct+pay@example.com\",\"amount\":1000}</payload>","intent":"immediate_retry"}]}
```

sophie (ML Eng): This is classic OpenAI-envelope vs Redwood-tool spec mismatch. OpenAI-compatible proxies sometimes stringify `arguments` and escape <,> as entities when shuttling through HTML layers. Also some clients send lowercase enum values. Two separate problems: (1) arguments type mismatch (string vs object) and (2) enum canonicalization for routing. Both cause our validator to reject.

sophie (ML Eng): Quick repro on local: send args as string and set intent lowercase -> validator bails at schema stage. I can reproduce with the snippet.

kevin (Support): Customer says this worked previously with their older proxy. they pushed a config change that toggled an XML sanitizer.

derek (Eng): Proposed immediate mitigation: compat shim in ingress that attempts to parse `arguments` if it's a string — try JSON.parse after unescaping common HTML entities (&lt; &gt; &amp;). Also map known enum aliases to our canonical ones (case-insensitive map). That should be low-risk and rollable as a hotfix.

derek (Eng): Example pseudo-patch:
```js
// ingress compat layer
function normalizeToolCall(tc){
  if(typeof tc.arguments === 'string'){
    const unescaped = tc.arguments.replace(/&lt;/g,'<').replace(/&gt;/g,'>').replace(/&amp;/g,'&');
    try{ tc.arguments = JSON.parse(unescaped); }catch(e){ /* leave as-is, will be handled by validator downstream */ }
  }
  if(typeof tc.intent === 'string'){
    const mapping = { 'immediate_retry':'IMMEDIATE', 'defer':'DEFERRED' };
    const key = tc.intent.toLowerCase();
    if(mapping[key]) tc.intent = mapping[key];
    else tc.intent = tc.intent.toUpperCase();
  }
  return tc;
}
```

maya (Support): Customer is happy to test a patch in staging. they can send sample traffic.

sophie (ML Eng): Also add a telemetry counter for how often `arguments` arrives as string and how often enum aliasing occurs — helps product decide whether to permanently accept these variants.

derek (Eng): Logging note: capture original raw payload + normalized payload for 24h then drop. add feature flag to enable shim per-tenant.

kevin (Support): Filed CS ticket CS-4381 and assigned to eng-runtime. customer contact: jane@acctcorp, severity P2, wants staging link.

derek (Eng): I'll open PR with the shim + unit tests (parsing edge cases) and a canary rollout to staging. tagging @sophie for enum mapping review.

sophie (ML Eng): For enum mapping, prefer explicit whitelist mapping rather than toUpperCase fallback for unknowns — avoids collisions. I will drop a small mapping list in PR.

maya (Support): Thanks everyone. keeping customer posted: will share staging URL once PR merges. :thumbsup:

ingest-bot: deployment to staging started for rev-7723 (canary route for tenant acctcorp).

kevin (Support): follow-ups: (1) confirm billing transactions unaffected, (2) validate no performance regression (latency) with shim, (3) add short KB entry for customers using openai proxies.

derek (Eng): noted. will include perf numbers in PR.

maya (Support): closing loop here after staging test. will update CS-4381.
